          "chord-progressions.txt": textFile(
            `COMMON CHORD PROGRESSIONS\n=========================\n\nI - V - vi - IV      pop (C G Am F)\nI - IV - V           rock, blues, country (C F G)\nvi - IV - I - V      pop variation (Am F C G)\nii - V - I           jazz cadence (Dm7 G7 Cmaj7)\nI - vi - IV - V      50s doo wop (C Am F G)\nI - bVII - IV        mixolydian rock (D C G)\ni - bVII - bVI - V   andalusian (Am G F E)\n\n12 bar blues in A:\n| A7 | A7 | A7 | A7 |\n| D7 | D7 | A7 | A7 |\n| E7 | D7 | A7 | E7 |\n\nQuick blues turnaround: last bar goes to E7 to lead back to the top.\n\nNashville numbers: describe progressions by degree so they work in any key.`,
          ),
          "pentatonic-and-blues.txt": textFile(
            `PENTATONIC AND BLUES SCALES\n===========================\n\nMinor pentatonic: 1 b3 4 5 b7\nA minor pentatonic: A C D E G\n\nMajor pentatonic: 1 2 3 5 6\nA major pentatonic: A B C# E F#\n\nBlues scale: minor pentatonic plus the b5 (blue note)\nA blues: A C D Eb E G\n\nBox 1 of A minor pentatonic (5th fret position):\ne|-5--8-|\nB|-5--8-|\nG|-5--7-|\nD|-5--7-|\nA|-5--7-|\nE|-5--8-|\n\nRelative major and minor pentatonics share the same shapes. A minor pent is the same set of notes as C major pent.\n\nTechniques: bends, slides, hammer ons, pull offs, vibrato. Target chord tones on strong beats.`,
          ),
          "fretboard-and-caged.txt": textFile(
            `FRETBOARD KNOWLEDGE AND CAGED\n=============================\n\nStandard tuning (low to high): E A D G B E\n\nOctave shapes: same note two strings up and two frets over (E string 3rd fret G, D string 5th fret G).\n\nNatural notes on the low E string: E(0) F(1) G(3) A(5) B(7) C(8) D(10) E(12)\nOn the A string: A(0) B(2) C(3) D(5) E(7) F(8) G(10) A(12)\n\nCAGED system: five open chord shapes (C A G E D) that can be moved up the neck with a barre. Each shape links to a scale position.\n\nChord shape order moving up the neck for a given key: C, A, G, E, D, then repeats.\n\nUse CAGED to connect chords, scales and arpeggios across the whole neck.`,
          ),
          "rhythm-and-timing.txt": textFile(
            `RHYTHM AND TIMING\n=================\n\nTime signatures: 4/4 (most common), 3/4 (waltz), 6/8 (compound), 12/8 (slow blues).\n\nNote values: whole, half, quarter, eighth, sixteenth. Triplets divide the beat in three.\n\nCounting:\nQuarter notes: 1 2 3 4\nEighth notes: 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 &\nSixteenth notes: 1 e & a 2 e & a\n\nStrumming pattern (down and up): D DU UDU\n\nPractice with a metronome on beats 2 and 4 to develop a backbeat feel.\nMute strings with the fretting hand and palm to keep rhythm tight.\nFunk strumming relies on 16th note ghost strums and muted strings.`,
