          "repertoire.txt": textFile(
            `REPERTOIRE\n==========\n\nBlues:\n- Pride and Joy\n- The Thrill Is Gone\n- Red House\n\nRock:\n- Little Wing\n- Wish You Were Here\n- Under the Bridge\n- Sweet Child O' Mine (intro)\n\nPop and funk:\n- Superstition (rhythm)\n- Sultans of Swing (in progress)\n- Gravity (working on the phrasing)\n\nGoal: build a set of 10 songs I can play from memory.`,
          ),
          "techniques.txt": textFile(
            `TECHNIQUE NOTES\n===============\n\nBending: push with the ring finger backed up by the middle and index. Reach the target pitch and check it against the note on the neck.\n\nVibrato: wide and slow for blues, narrow and quick for rock.\n\nHybrid picking: pick and middle finger together for country style.\n\nDouble stops: play two notes together, great for Chuck Berry style rhythm.\n\nPalm muting: rest the edge of the picking hand lightly at the bridge.\n\nStrat tone tricks:\n- Position 2 and 4 (quack) for funk and clean tones\n- Roll the tone down for warm blues tone\n- Use the volume control to clean up a dirty amp\n- Tremolo arm for subtle vibrato`,
          ),
          "songs-to-learn.txt": textFile(
            `SONGS TO LEARN\n==============\n\n- Cliffs of Dover\n- Comfortably Numb (solos)\n- Texas Flood\n- Hotel California (solo)\n- Purple Rain\n- Voodoo Child (Slight Return)\n- Sultans of Swing\n- Johnny B. Goode\n- Cold Shot\n- Mr. Crowley\n\nPick one per month and work it up properly.`,
